# Pinned, EXPIRING exemptions from the Go module floors (go-modfloor.mk).
# Read by GOTC-05 (tests/ga_tests/run_build_tests.sh) via ga_go_modfloor_verdict and
# held to pinned constants by tests/ga_tests/build/go_toolchain/inputs_check.sh
# (GOTC-IN-10): entries, versions and the latest allowed expiry live THERE, so
# editing this file alone cannot extend or widen an exemption.
#
# An exemption allows exactly one binary to embed exactly one module at exactly the
# pinned version below its floor. It is void - and the gate goes red - when
#   * the expiry date has passed (even if the binary no longer needs it), or
#   * the binary embeds that module at any other version (a runc bump forces a re-look).
#
# BINARY-PATH|MODULE|PINNED-VERSION|ADVISORY-IDS|EXPIRES|REASON
usr/bin/runc|golang.org/x/net|v0.43.0|GO-2026-4440,GO-2026-4441,GO-2026-4918,GO-2026-5025,GO-2026-5026,GO-2026-5027,GO-2026-5028,GO-2026-5029,GO-2026-5030,GO-2026-5942,GO-2026-6603,GO-2026-6610,GO-2026-6611,GO-2026-6612,GO-2026-6617|2026-11-30|runc 1.4.3 (cgo, tags static_build seccomp) imports only golang.org/x/net/bpf from x/net; every listed advisory is module-level only, govulncheck source and binary mode report none of them as called (2026-10-13); bumping x/net made runc 1.4.3 fail to compile in the BOSv1.5.1-rc3 bake (unknown field IsDefault in config.Device); re-evaluate on the next runc bump or at expiry
